        <mxCell id="c131" value="&lt;i&gt;Rows 1 and 2 are scrolled out of view. The average lag is above the median: a minority of orders take much longer. Outlined: the promotions whose dates cannot span their sales (promotion 1 lasts one day; promotion 4 ends before it starts; promotion 7 ends before it starts); every line of them falls after the end date, so the 100 percent says nothing about billing. The other 6 promotions have between 28% and 50% of their lines invoiced after the end date.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="434" width="860" height="64" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
